 it never exercises the second gate_key and would not catch the duplicate emission"],"finding":"The 'warn once' guarantee holds only per-gate-key, not 'once per overlay content' as the Context asserts: the warn is placed inside _effective_routing_cached, whose lru_cache key is (gate_key, rr, overlay_sig), so an overlay evaluated for both plan_review and code_review gates emits the deprecation twice.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd58aaabf6d954ee7","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / Context ('rides the existing (gate_key, repo_root, overlay-signature) lru_cache ... to fire once per overlay content')","norm_id":"n051bbdea51b88552","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A client project whose .rebar/criteria_routing.json uses the list form runs both `rebar review` (plan_review) and `rebar review-code` (code_review) in one process, emitting the deprecation twice despite a 'warn once' intent"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either reword Context/step 2 to say the warn fires once per (gate_key, overlay) — matching the cache key — or hang the dedupe off an overlay-signature-only cache (e.g. a separate @lru_cache keyed on overlay_sig) so it is genuinely once per overlay content; and extend the test to call once with gate_key='code_review' to document the chosen behaviour.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt